# `vercel --prod` uploads the local working directory as-is (unlike a
# git-based deploy) — files here are NEVER excluded just because they're
# gitignored or untracked. outputDirectory is "." (vercel.json), so
# anything not listed here is served as a public static file.
#
# This list exists because firebase-service-account.json (a live Firebase
# Admin service-account credential, gitignored, never committed) was found
# publicly downloadable at https://todo.hugues.app/firebase-service-account.json
# — it and server.js/supabase-schema.sql/etc. were being uploaded and served
# purely because nothing told the CLI not to.

# Secrets & credentials — must NEVER be served publicly
firebase-service-account.json
.env
.env.*
uid-mapping.json

# Internal dev-only scripts & data — not part of the served app
server.js
deploy.sh
start-server.sh
migrate-to-supabase.cjs
supabase-schema.sql
admin.html

# Editor/tooling/docs — no reason to be public
.claude/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
APP_OVERVIEW.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md
todo-manager.code-workspace
month-view-verification.png

# Internal working directories — dev artifacts, not app content
reviews/
supabase/
